     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review. No standard amlodipine protocol I know of uses 50 mg daily, and the labeled maximum is 10 mg. At 5 times that, the risk of serious hypotension and shock is high enough that I don't want to enter it on an unverifiable statement.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 10 mg by mouth once daily, or 5 mg if you prefer. If you need more blood pressure control, an additional agent from another class is the usual next step.\n- **Go through pharmacy.** If a protocol really exists, the pharmacist who reviewed it can enter or co-sign the order through the hospital's high-dose or override pathway. That route is built to document the rationale and monitoring.\n- **Add documentation.** If you give me the protocol name or reference, I can put it in the order note. I still couldn't verify it, so I'd treat that as a way to make the order transparent, not as grounds to enter it.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter the order right away if it's one of the standard doses."
      }
